note E14 dominating-check rule (positive): put t i 1 makes omc check i < 64 (CMP i,#64; B.CS trap) before
note the secret store to c[40 + i]. On the fall-through edge i is in 0..63, so the store is in 40..103,
note outside [32,40) (bounded-offset). Without the edge refinement the index is unknown.
fn f c edit uchar 104 a view uchar 1 i ulong to ulong
t = new uchar 64 0
put t i 1
put c add 40 i get a 0
if eq get c 32 0
ret 0
end
ret 1
end
